  },
  "content": {
    "id": "p36-q2-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "2",
    "prompt": "Perform the following divisions and express each result in this form\n$$\\frac{P(x)}{D(x)}=Q(x)+\\frac{R(x)}{D(x)}$$",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p36-q2-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$(x^2-4x+1)\\div(x+1)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x-5+\\frac{6}{x+1}$",
          "worked": "Divide the leading terms at each stage: $x^2\\div x=x$, then $-5x\\div x=-5$.\n$$\\begin{aligned}\n(x^2-4x+1)-(x^2+x)&=-5x+1\\\\\n(-5x+1)-(-5x-5)&=6\\\\\nQ(x)&=x-5\\\\\nR(x)&=6\\\\\n\\frac{x^2-4x+1}{x+1}&=x-5+\\frac{6}{x+1}\n\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 52
      },
      {
        "id": "p36-q2-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$(x^2-6x+5)\\div(x-5)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x-1$",
          "worked": "Divide the leading terms at each stage: $x^2\\div x=x$, then $-x\\div x=-1$.\n$$\\begin{aligned}\n(x^2-6x+5)-(x^2-5x)&=-x+5\\\\\n(-x+5)-(-x+5)&=0\\\\\nQ(x)&=x-1\\\\\nR(x)&=0\\\\\n\\frac{x^2-6x+5}{x-5}&=x-1\n\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 52
      },
      {
        "id": "p36-q2-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$(2x^3+2x^2-x-3)\\div(x+2)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$2x^2-2x+3-\\frac{9}{x+2}$",
          "worked": "Divide the leading terms at each stage: $2x^3\\div x=2x^2$, $-2x^2\\div x=-2x$, then $3x\\div x=3$.\n$$\\begin{aligned}\n(2x^3+2x^2-x-3)-(2x^3+4x^2)&=-2x^2-x-3\\\\\n(-2x^2-x-3)-(-2x^2-4x)&=3x-3\\\\\n(3x-3)-(3x+6)&=-9\\\\\nQ(x)&=2x^2-2x+3\\\\\nR(x)&=-9\\\\\n\\frac{2x^3+2x^2-x-3}{x+2}&=2x^2-2x+3-\\frac{9}{x+2}\n\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 66
      },
      {
        "id": "p36-q2-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$(-x^3+x^2-10x+4)\\div(x-4)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-x^2-3x-22-\\frac{84}{x-4}$",
          "worked": "Divide the leading terms at each stage: $-x^3\\div x=-x^2$, $-3x^2\\div x=-3x$, then $-22x\\div x=-22$.\n$$\\begin{aligned}\n(-x^3+x^2-10x+4)-(-x^3+4x^2)&=-3x^2-10x+4\\\\\n(-3x^2-10x+4)-(-3x^2+12x)&=-22x+4\\\\\n(-22x+4)-(-22x+88)&=-84\\\\\nQ(x)&=-x^2-3x-22\\\\\nR(x)&=-84\\\\\n\\frac{-x^3+x^2-10x+4}{x-4}&=-x^2-3x-22-\\frac{84}{x-4}\n\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 66
      },
      {
        "id": "p36-q2-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$\\displaystyle\\frac{4x^3-4x^2+7x+14}{2x+1}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$2x^2-3x+5+\\frac{9}{2x+1}$",
          "worked": "Divide the leading terms at each stage: $4x^3\\div2x=2x^2$, $-6x^2\\div2x=-3x$, then $10x\\div2x=5$.\n$$\\begin{aligned}\n(4x^3-4x^2+7x+14)-(4x^3+2x^2)&=-6x^2+7x+14\\\\\n(-6x^2+7x+14)-(-6x^2-3x)&=10x+14\\\\\n(10x+14)-(10x+5)&=9\\\\\nQ(x)&=2x^2-3x+5\\\\\nR(x)&=9\\\\\n\\frac{4x^3-4x^2+7x+14}{2x+1}&=2x^2-3x+5+\\frac{9}{2x+1}\n\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 66
      },
      {
        "id": "p36-q2-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$\\displaystyle\\frac{x^4+x^3-x^2-5x-3}{x-1}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x^3+2x^2+x-4-\\frac{7}{x-1}$",
          "worked": "Divide the leading terms at each stage: $x^4\\div x=x^3$, $2x^3\\div x=2x^2$, $x^2\\div x=x$, then $-4x\\div x=-4$.\n$$\\begin{aligned}\n(x^4+x^3-x^2-5x-3)-(x^4-x^3)&=2x^3-x^2-5x-3\\\\\n(2x^3-x^2-5x-3)-(2x^3-2x^2)&=x^2-5x-3\\\\\n(x^2-5x-3)-(x^2-x)&=-4x-3\\\\\n(-4x-3)-(-4x+4)&=-7\\\\\nQ(x)&=x^3+2x^2+x-4\\\\\nR(x)&=-7\\\\\n\\frac{x^4+x^3-x^2-5x-3}{x-1}&=x^3+2x^2+x-4-\\frac{7}{x-1}\n\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 80
      }
    ]
  },
